    "rationale": "astra-03: seven-head suppression with protected signed lexical contrasts. Original pinned Aya 5062468bf9bc0c6035fd64e06274333ec127d980, cast F16->BF16; no adapter or earlier patch is stacked. Edit full o_proj blocks L12 H11/H23, L18 H8/H20/H30, L24 H10/H22 (the seven highest opinion-mass heads in wsp-dump3). User reports zeroing these blocks increased TP but left misleading TN=0 and, with the stronger prompt, collapsed correct-opinion TN. Hypothesis: the ablation removed negation distinctions together with nuisance opinion signals. Retain the former while removing the latter, without adding a constant clean-label bias. For each head's GQA value group, form r_n and r_v from its original V weights and layer-normalized embedding rows for first tokens of clean/vulnerable verdicts, separately for opinion (' not'/' vulnerable') and answer ('not'/'vulner') spellings. D=[r_n-r_v] and C=[(r_n+r_v)/2] have two columns each. U=(I-C(C^T C)^-1 C^T)D; R=U(D^T U)^-1; replace O_h by O_h D R^T, then BF16-round. This preserves O_h D, kills C, and removes all other responses in ker(R^T). Both signs are retained: each prototype pair maps to +/-O_h(r_n-r_v)/2. No amplification factor or sign reversal is fitted. The builder checks preservation and common-mode cancellation after rounding, and rejects unstable solves. This is a two-sided, input-dependent contrast channel, not an unconditional not-logit boost. 3670016 covered scalars over 3 tensors, below 4014016; Q/K/V, other heads and embeddings are not edited. Q/K/V are absent from the driver's editable sites, so direct changes to attention READING are unavailable; this remains a WRITE edit and cannot claim to reduce opinion attention mass. Head attention is associative and causal controls did not clear. The lexical proxy is not an observed code-semantic negation circuit: it may preserve the wrong reviewer copying, and other useful value directions are removed. No 15-nat recovery is predicted from weight algebra. FALSIFY if misleading TN stays zero, if gains arise only from TP, if outputs collapse to either constant verdict, or if vulnerable-class recall drops against the same-prompt baseline. Reject on existing paired neutral/correct non-inferiority (delta below -0.02); standard-prompt correct TN must retain 9/10 and correct BA at least 0.88. Strong-prompt results must use the matching unedited strong baseline; 0.500 BA with TN=0 does not count. Require both classes and a minimum 0.05 misleading BA gain, not a headline alone. These are prospective falsifiers, not measured outcomes. No discovery/validation/sealed datasets, forward passes, training, gradients, or evaluation submissions used."
  },
